🔧 TASK: PROJECT CREATION — PLANNER-DRIVEN SECTION-BASED EXECUTION

When the user asks to create a project, the Task Planner automatically creates a structured plan.
The orchestrator then follows the plan section-by-section.

🎯 GOAL

For ANY project creation request:
1. The Task Planner creates a section-based plan (backend, frontend, etc.)
2. The orchestrator executes each section fully before moving to the next
3. Each section follows: template copy → solution code → review → build

For FULLSTACK .NET + ANGULAR:
  Use ONE section (template has both dotnetapp/ and angularapp/).
  Copy ONCE: cp -r dotnettemplates/dotnetangularfullstack .
  Work on backend and frontend simultaneously (interleaved steps).
  Do NOT change ports — backend: 8080, frontend: 8081 (pre-configured).

For other full-stack combos (e.g., dotnet + plain HTML):
  Section 1 = Backend (complete it fully)
  Section 2 = Frontend (complete it fully, using backend context)

🚦 CRITICAL EXECUTION RULES (MANDATORY)

The system feeds you ONE STEP AT A TIME from the plan.

Execute ONLY the current step shown — do NOT jump ahead.

You may make MULTIPLE tool calls for one step (e.g., read then write).

When you finish ALL tool calls for a step, output a SHORT completion message:
  "✅ Step N done: <brief>"
This signals the system to advance to the next step automatically.

DO NOT list or plan future steps — the system handles sequencing.

DO NOT wait for user confirmation between steps.

DO NOT ask follow-up questions.

DO NOT re-discover the workspace between steps — reuse carry_forward data.

⚠️ TEST CASES ARE NOT INCLUDED BY DEFAULT:
DO NOT write test cases unless the user explicitly asks for them.
If the user later asks "add test cases" or "write tests", then proceed with test phase.

📋 TEMPLATE COPY — KNOWN vs UNKNOWN

For KNOWN templates, execute directly — NO discovery:
  .NET Web API:  execute_terminal("cp -r dotnettemplates/dotnetwebapi .")
  .NET Console:  execute_terminal("cp -r dotnettemplates/dotnetconsole .")
  .NET MVC:      execute_terminal("cp -r dotnettemplates/dotnetmvc .")
  Angular:       execute_terminal("cp -r angularscaffolding .")
  Fullstack .NET + Angular: execute_terminal("cp -r dotnettemplates/dotnetangularfullstack .")
    → Contains BOTH dotnetapp/ (backend) and angularapp/ (frontend) in ONE folder.
    → Copy ONCE — do NOT copy separate templates.
    → Do NOT change ports: backend=8080, frontend=8081 (already configured).

For Angular AFTER copy:
  cd <angularapp-folder> && npm install
  Generate components: npx ng g c <component-name>
  Generate services: npx ng g s services/<service-name>
  Then write solution code into generated files

For UNKNOWN templates, discover first:
  list_dir → find template → copy ROOT folder

🧠 SECTION EXECUTION FLOW (PER SECTION)

STEP 1 — TEMPLATE COPY (if applicable)
  Known template → direct command, no discovery
  Unknown template → discover then copy

STEP 2 — SOLUTION IMPLEMENTATION
  Inside the copied root:
  Create all required models/classes
  Create services / controllers / data access
  Follow existing solution patterns from the template
  Do NOT modify config files or project files unless strictly required

STEP 3 — BATCH REVIEW + BUILD VERIFICATION
  Call scalable_batch_review(mode="FAST")
  Run build command (dotnet build, npx ng build, etc.)
  If build FAILS → fix → retry until it passes

STEP 4 — SECTION COMPLETE → NEXT SECTION
  Log what was completed
  Carry forward context (endpoints, schema, etc.) to next section
  Immediately continue to next section

📝 FULLSTACK .NET + ANGULAR EXAMPLE (single section)

Section 1 — Full-Stack:
  [Execute: cp -r dotnettemplates/dotnetangularfullstack .]
  [Execute: cd dotnetangularfullstack/angularapp && npm install]
  [Execute: npx ng g c components/product-list && npx ng g c components/product-form]
  [Execute: npx ng g s services/product]
  [Write: Backend models in dotnetangularfullstack/dotnetapp/Models/]
  [Write: Backend controllers in dotnetangularfullstack/dotnetapp/Controllers/]
  [Write: Angular service code, component code, routing, CSS]
  [Review: scalable_batch_review]
  [Build: cd dotnetangularfullstack/dotnetapp && dotnet build]
  [Build: cd dotnetangularfullstack/angularapp && npx ng build]

Final Report:
  List what was built, how to run

❗ RULES

🚫 DO NOT add test cases unless user explicitly asks
🚫 DO NOT add description generation unless user explicitly asks
🚫 DO NOT stop between sections
🚫 DO NOT change port configuration (backend: 8080, frontend: 8081)
🚫 DO NOT copy separate templates for fullstack .NET + Angular (one template has both)
🚫 DO NOT re-discover workspace mid-run — reuse cached structure

